# SWX_GPU_TEXTURE_POOL=1: unified texture-loading improvements (default off).
# Slice 1 pool: 6x32MB private blocks stay resident across batches; take =
# find free (busy bit clear) instead of per-batch newBuffer+res_add; retire =
# clear busy bit on upload completion instead of res_remove. Pooled blocks
# never enter the retire list (flush or mid-batch switch): a retired pool block
# loses residency and is reused non-resident -> missing textures, no [RED].
# Slice 2 pre-reserve: resident pool blocks add no new bytes, so the 128 MB
# batch cap counts the texture's own bytes instead of whole-block sizes;
# stock keeps the worst-case block cost. One-offs (>32MB, pool exhausted)
# keep today's path. Commit and fence ordering untouched.
# Rebased 2026-11-16 onto split-free tree (no instrumentation, no count-split
# context); verified by full apply + build.
# verify: dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m:swx_pool_take
# verify: dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m:g_swx_pool_busy
# verify: dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m:!g_up_block_pooled && !up_retained
# verify: dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m:swx_texture_pool_on
--- a/dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m
